    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the shape of this trip, and so do I. On TRP-00111 (Woodlands to one-north, morning of 3 August 2026) the booked optimal was 24.0 km and the trace measures 29.98 km — an excess of 5.98 km, 24.92%. That clears both of POL-RD-01's establishment gates (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so the rider is right that a deviation exists, and the governing distance is the trace's 29.98 km, not the trip record's rounded 30.0 km convenience copy. The excess is, however, below the materiality gate (50% or 8.0 km), so no POL-RD-06 driver-profile inquiry arises on this trip.\n\nThe driver's exoneration under POL-RD-03 succeeds in full. LTA advisory ADV-20260803-014 (EV-ADVIS-00111-01) closes the PIE towards Tuas between Clementi Rd and Jalan Anak Bukit — the very expressway segment the optimal route traverses — from 07:10 to 09:30, bracketing the whole trip, and the trace (EV-GPS-00111) shows the vehicle leaving that corridor at Bukit Panjang before the closed segment and rejoining on the AYE. The clause caps the exoneration, so the rider is right to ask for the cap to be run: justified excess = min(5.98, 1.30 x (29.2 - 24.0) + 1.00) = min(5.98, 7.76) = 5.98 km. The whole measured excess sits inside the cap, so no excess survives for POL-RD-02 to refund. The rider's argument that the cap must leave something refundable fails on the record's own figures — the cap is larger than the excess.\n\nEven run against the closure-adjusted optimal (29.98 km, 37.5 minutes), the arithmetic confirms it: recomputed fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 29.98 + 0.28 x 37.5) x 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, the only artifact that carries it, + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP = SGD 37.585, against a charged total of SGD 37.74. The difference, about SGD 0.16, is below the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor, so POL-RD-02 yields NO_ACTION in any event. The rider's alternative computation against the unadjusted 24.0 km optimum (SGD 31.00, an alleged SGD 6.74 overcharge) is rejected: once POL-RD-03 applies, POL-RD-02 must run against the closure-adjusted route, not the booked one.\n\nNo pass-through correction is due under POL-RD-09: the fare breakdown carries tolls_erp of 0.00 and an empty erp_gantries list, so there is nothing to settle and no billing-integrity defect. No rider-requested detour arises under POL-RD-04 — the rider's only message fixed an arrival time and named no road or waypoint, so the corroboration test cannot run. POL-RD-05 and POL-RD-12 are not in play: no pickup or dropoff was amended and the vehicle was RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL. The rider's later recollection that she 'did not see any closure' cites no artifact and does not outweigh a timestamped government record covering the disputed segment. Every artifact the ruling rests on carries full weight (1.0), so no discount applies and nothing here needs a human reviewer. The fare stands as charged; the disputed SGD 8.00 is not refunded."
